# Extra --env-file paths, one per line, relative to this directory, applied in
# order BEFORE this stack's own .env so its values win.
#
# These are compose INTERPOLATION sources, not env_file: entries -- nothing here
# is injected into the container. The console displays which model and endpoint
# AgentMemory is configured for, and the authority on that is the agentmemory
# stack's .env. Reading it here keeps one copy of the truth; the alternative was
# a second set of LLM_* values in this stack's .env that silently went stale.
#
# The distinction is load-bearing: an env_file: entry WOULD hand the console
# OPENAI_API_KEY, and the console is deliberately never given a provider secret.
../agentmemory/.env
